Hi Daniel,

It looks like you may be using a version of mirt that is out of date (the error I got first was that the 'itemtype' argument was missing). So I would recommend updating (version 1.10 is the latest) and trying the following code instead:

```

library(mirt)
a <- matrix(c(1.5, NA, 0.5, NA, 1, NA, 1, 0.5, NA, 1.5, NA, 0.5,
              NA, 1, NA, 1), ncol = 2, byrow = TRUE)

d <- matrix(c(-1, NA, NA, -1.5, NA, NA, 1.5, NA, NA, 0, NA, NA,
              3, 2, -0.5, 2.5, 1, -1, 2, 0, NA, 1, NA, NA),
            ncol = 3, byrow = TRUE)

sigma <- diag(2)
sigma[1, 2] <- sigma[2, 1] <- 0.4

itemtype <- rep('dich', 8)
itemtype[5:7] <- 'graded'
simdata2 <- simdata(a, d, 2000, sigma, itemtype = itemtype)
```

Cheers.

Phil

