Subject: Re: nested or non-nested
Message-ID: <kLpBo2pdCFk.QUAAcyRE5-AJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <kLpBo2pdCFk.IJa1UXeMgVMJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
References: <kLpBo2pdCFk.IJa1UXeMgVMJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/mirt-package/c/kLpBo2pdCFk/m/QUAAcyRE5-AJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Non-nested, so you can only compare with AIC, BIC, etc, and fit model statistics. And no there is no rule of thumb for a factor loading. Even the original cutoffs had no real basis for being set. It's exploratory data analysis, so use your discretion.

Phil

